For sentiment analysis, we can use a pre-trained sentiment analysis model such as VADER (Valence Aware Dictionary and sEntiment Reasoner) to analyze the sentiment of each message in the conversation. VADER is a rule-based sentiment analysis tool that uses a lexicon of words and phrases with known sentiment polarity to determine the overall sentiment of a text. We can use a library like NLTK (Natural Language Toolkit) to load the VADER model and apply it to the conversation data to obtain sentiment scores for each message.
